       ~ setrec1lem3 .)  Therefore, by ~ setrec1lem4 , ` ( F `` A ) ` is a
       subset of some set recursively generated by ` F ` .  Thus, by ~ ssuni ,
       it is a subset of the union of all sets recursively generated by ` F ` .

       See ~ df-setrecs for a detailed description of how the ` setrecs `
       definition works.

